From: Daniele Masato <daniele.masato@pm.me>
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: sophgo: cv18xx: support bias-disable

The cv18xx pad registers have separate pull-up and pull-down enables, but
the driver only accepts bias-pull-up and bias-pull-down, and rejects any
other parameter, which fails the whole pin state. A pad that must float
cannot be described: the SG2002 MIPI RX pads reset with an 87 kOhm
pull-down that stays on the CSI lanes.

Accept bias-disable: clear both enables, and report it when neither is set.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/sophgo/pinctrl-cv18xx.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/sophgo/pinctrl-cv18xx.c
@@ -260,6 +260,10 @@
 	value = readl(cv1800_pinctrl_get_component_addr(priv, &pin->conf));
 
 	switch (param) {
+	case PIN_CONFIG_BIAS_DISABLE:
+		enabled = !(value & (PIN_IO_PULLUP | PIN_IO_PULLDOWN));
+		arg = 0;
+		break;
 	case PIN_CONFIG_BIAS_PULL_DOWN:
 		enabled = FIELD_GET(PIN_IO_PULLDOWN, value);
 		arg = sophgo_pinctrl_typical_pull_down(pctrl, sp, priv->power_cfg);
@@ -330,6 +334,10 @@
 		u32 arg = pinconf_to_config_argument(configs[i]);
 
 		switch (param) {
+		case PIN_CONFIG_BIAS_DISABLE:
+			v &= ~(PIN_IO_PULLUP | PIN_IO_PULLDOWN);
+			m |= PIN_IO_PULLUP | PIN_IO_PULLDOWN;
+			break;
 		case PIN_CONFIG_BIAS_PULL_DOWN:
 			v &= ~PIN_IO_PULLDOWN;
 			v |= FIELD_PREP(PIN_IO_PULLDOWN, arg);
